= 2.1 Overview

As part of a summer camp organized by Akanksha Charitable Trust, Puttur, with VCET, Puttur, and Tata Consultancy Services (TCS), this activity supported the educational development of rural students. It was held from 05-05-2025 to 17-05-2025 and aimed to introduce useful digital skills while motivating students to think about higher education and future careers.

The camp covered practical and productivity-oriented topics including HTML, CSS, Canva, Office Tools, G-Suite, and the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Demonstrations, discussions, and interactive exercises were used to make these topics accessible and useful to the participating students.

Through HTML and CSS, the students learned how a basic web page is structured and styled. Canva activities encouraged them to create posters, presentations, and other digital material, while Office Tools and G-Suite demonstrations improved their familiarity with everyday productivity platforms.

The students were also encouraged to take part in a hackathon. Guidance was provided on identifying problems, developing ideas, working in teams, and presenting solutions, allowing them to apply their new knowledge in a practical setting.

Sessions on the Sustainable Development Goals connected technology learning with social, economic, and environmental concerns. The discussions and activities helped the students become more confident and interested in continued learning.

Overall, the summer camp successfully contributed to improving the digital literacy, creativity, communication, problem-solving ability, and confidence of rural students. The activity also encouraged students to explore technology as a tool for education and future career development.

= 2.2 Use of Technology

#block(spacing: 12pt)[Digital tools and platforms were used throughout the camp to make the sessions practical and interactive. The following technological aspects were covered:]

- Training students in HTML and CSS for basic web page development.
- Demonstration of Canva for designing posters, presentations, and creative content.
- Use of Microsoft Office tools for preparing documents and presentations.
- Introduction to G-Suite/Google Workspace and its productivity applications.
- Use of digital presentations and practical demonstrations to make learning interactive.
- Guidance on using technology for hackathon idea development and presentation.
- Use of online and digital learning resources to encourage independent learning.

= 2.3 Sustainable Development Best Practices

#block(spacing: 12pt)[The activity supported the following sustainable development practices:]

- Promoting Quality Education (SDG 4) by providing digital and technical education to rural students.
- Reducing the digital knowledge gap by improving access to basic technology skills.
- Encouraging students to use technology for education, creativity, and problem-solving.
- Creating awareness about the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).
- Developing communication, teamwork, creativity, and confidence among students.
- Encouraging rural students to explore higher education and technology-oriented careers.
- Promoting responsible and productive use of digital tools.

= 2.4 Outcome of the Activity

The summer camp provided rural students with practical exposure to essential digital and productivity tools. Students gained basic knowledge of web development, digital designing, office applications, and online collaboration tools. The hackathon guidance further helped them improve their problem-solving, teamwork, creativity, and presentation skills. The programme successfully enhanced their digital awareness and encouraged them to consider technology and higher education as pathways for their future development.

